SHADOW MODEL
A provisional transition-duration predictor.

The model uses:
current local context features

to estimate:
developmental duration.

Primary adversarial condition:

BASE

approximately calibrated.

DAMAGED/SLOW

systematically underestimates duration by:
~2.5 steps
before calibration.

REUSED/FAST

systematically OVERestimates duration by:
~6 steps

with:
low prediction noise.

This last condition is deliberately dangerous.

The shadow model believes:
development is still expensive

when:
the organism has actually become:
fast to develop.

