DECISION
AR-H95 is POSITIVE WITH A MODEL-SELF-DELUSION LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- model-based rehearsal can reduce live developmental audit cost;
- a stale shadow model can strongly misprice development;
- pessimistic shadow predictions can prevent the live evidence needed to correct them;
- sparse real calibration restores self-model accuracy;
- shadow + sparse calibration approaches the value of much more frequent live auditing;
- perfectly calibrated shadow rehearsal is a strong upper bound.

Not demonstrated:

- real developmental simulation;
- model construction from current Yggdrasil state;
- safe counterfactual execution;
- multi-model uncertainty;
- distributed shadow rehearsal;
- offline/dormant rehearsal.

